1
00:00:06,342 --> 00:00:08,789
"If you think you understand
quantum mechanics,

2
00:00:08,869 --> 00:00:11,317
you don't understand quantum mechanics."

3
00:00:11,397 --> 00:00:14,011
Richard Feynman is said
to have quipped that.

4
00:00:14,822 --> 00:00:17,609
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

5
00:00:17,689 --> 00:00:21,880
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

6
00:00:22,698 --> 00:00:24,996
The same holds for dependent arising.

7
00:00:25,076 --> 00:00:27,514
If you think you understand it, you don't.

8
00:00:28,329 --> 00:00:31,469
I can agree that nothing
has an essence of its own.

9
00:00:31,549 --> 00:00:33,208
I can say so fluently.

10
00:00:33,288 --> 00:00:38,946
And still I hold the world exactly
as before. Solid. Out there. Mine.

11
00:00:39,757 --> 00:00:42,004
Agreeing is not living in it.

12
00:00:42,822 --> 00:00:44,604
So I will not argue first.

13
00:00:44,684 --> 00:00:47,647
I will set two ways of
seeing side by side,

14
00:00:47,727 --> 00:00:50,419
three times, as sharply as I can.

15
00:00:50,499 --> 00:00:52,407
Then we can ask which one holds.

16
00:00:53,273 --> 00:00:54,583
First, an apple.

17
00:00:55,777 --> 00:01:01,077
Look at it. I can toss it from hand to
hand. Hold it tightly. Bite into it.

18
00:01:01,157 --> 00:01:02,984
Nothing seems more plainly there.

19
00:01:03,797 --> 00:01:09,722
It appears undeniably objective.
External. Out there. Existing on its own.

20
00:01:09,802 --> 00:01:12,603
It was in the bowl before
I walked into the kitchen,

21
00:01:12,683 --> 00:01:16,692
with its own weight, its
own hardness, its own edge,

22
00:01:16,772 --> 00:01:18,599
drawn from its own side.

23
00:01:19,414 --> 00:01:21,060
That is innate grasping.

24
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:26,060
The naming disappears so completely into
what appears that the apple seems to stand

25
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:27,355
by itself.

26
00:01:28,165 --> 00:01:32,423
Or, and it is a big or, look
at how this apple is formed.

27
00:01:33,246 --> 00:01:37,568
Six streams of consciousness,
each dependently originated,

28
00:01:37,648 --> 00:01:41,581
meeting and interacting, and
named apple in the meeting.

29
00:01:42,394 --> 00:01:47,206
Touch. Coolness, firmness, the
pull of weight against my palm.

30
00:01:47,286 --> 00:01:50,494
These are not stored in the
fruit, waiting to be found.

31
00:01:50,574 --> 00:01:52,917
They arise as skin meets fruit.

32
00:01:53,737 --> 00:01:59,241
Seeing. Red, which turns orange
under candlelight, and grey at dusk.

33
00:01:59,321 --> 00:02:02,370
It arises with light, eye and attention.

34
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:06,313
Hearing. The crunch as
my teeth break the skin.

35
00:02:06,393 --> 00:02:10,584
That sound was never sitting inside
the apple, waiting to be let out.

36
00:02:11,385 --> 00:02:17,385
Smell and taste. Sweetness and tartness,
only when flesh meets tongue and breath.

37
00:02:18,493 --> 00:02:20,587
And mind. Recognising it.

38
00:02:20,667 --> 00:02:23,879
Remembering other apples. The name, apple.

39
00:02:24,702 --> 00:02:28,377
This is not what the apple
really is. It is how it forms.

40
00:02:29,181 --> 00:02:32,185
Each stream is complete
in its own conditions.

41
00:02:32,265 --> 00:02:35,976
None of the six ever meets
an apple standing on its own.

42
00:02:36,056 --> 00:02:38,910
What ties them into one
solid thing out there,

43
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:43,489
with a solid me in here tossing
it, is formation running on habit.

44
00:02:43,569 --> 00:02:46,388
So quick and smooth
that it goes unnoticed.

45
00:02:47,209 --> 00:02:49,792
And the streams are not
a bare layer underneath,

46
00:02:49,872 --> 00:02:52,210
given first and named later.

47
00:02:52,290 --> 00:02:55,960
The coolness, the red and the
crunch are designated too.

48
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:58,288
They are no more found than the apple.

49
00:02:59,093 --> 00:03:03,130
Nor are the six streams a factory
in here, producing the apple.

50
00:03:03,210 --> 00:03:05,534
Seeing arises with eye and colour.

51
00:03:05,614 --> 00:03:08,279
Touch arises with skin and contact.

52
00:03:08,359 --> 00:03:13,890
Consciousness is as dependently arisen,
and as unfindable, as the apple.

53
00:03:13,970 --> 00:03:16,757
The apple is not found
apart from the streams.

54
00:03:16,837 --> 00:03:18,691
And it is not made by them either.

55
00:03:19,497 --> 00:03:22,351
And even seen this way,
nothing is missing.

56
00:03:22,431 --> 00:03:26,251
The apple can still be
tossed, eaten, and nourish me.

57
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:29,122
Seeing how it forms takes
nothing away from it.

58
00:03:29,954 --> 00:03:31,550
Second, a mountain.

59
00:03:32,513 --> 00:03:34,172
It is massive and still.

60
00:03:34,252 --> 00:03:37,976
It was there long before me,
and it will be there long after.

61
00:03:38,056 --> 00:03:40,055
It does not move when I look away.

62
00:03:40,135 --> 00:03:43,510
It stops the climber, whether
or not he believes in it.

63
00:03:44,325 --> 00:03:48,158
If anything is undeniably
objective, external,

64
00:03:48,238 --> 00:03:51,912
and existing on its own,
surely it is the mountain.

65
00:03:52,742 --> 00:03:57,354
Or, and again it is a big or, look
at how this mountain is formed.

66
00:03:58,197 --> 00:04:01,677
From the valley, it is a
blue shape against the sky.

67
00:04:01,757 --> 00:04:06,270
On the path, it is the ache
in my legs, the thin cold air,

68
00:04:06,350 --> 00:04:08,348
the crunch of scree underfoot.

69
00:04:08,428 --> 00:04:12,144
On the map, it is contour
lines and a height in metres.

70
00:04:12,945 --> 00:04:16,560
And the name mountain draws an
edge where nature drew none.

71
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:19,663
Where does the mountain
stop, and the plain begin?

72
00:04:20,447 --> 00:04:23,424
Look for the mountain
among the rocks, the soil,

73
00:04:23,504 --> 00:04:28,673
the slopes and the tree line. It is not
among them. And it is not apart from them.

74
00:04:29,489 --> 00:04:31,546
When no one is looking, is it there?

75
00:04:32,362 --> 00:04:34,728
Two claims sound alike, and are not.

76
00:04:34,808 --> 00:04:38,845
It is still there when I look
away and look back. That is true.

77
00:04:38,925 --> 00:04:43,016
It is checked the ordinary way.
I look again. Others see it.

78
00:04:43,096 --> 00:04:45,154
The road is still there to drive on.

79
00:04:45,961 --> 00:04:50,473
It exists from its own side, whether
or not anything ever meets it.

80
00:04:50,553 --> 00:04:53,367
That is a different claim.
And nothing has earned it.

81
00:04:53,447 --> 00:04:56,918
It slips in because the first
claim works so reliably.

82
00:04:57,738 --> 00:05:00,828
But being reliable is
not being independent.

83
00:05:01,641 --> 00:05:04,509
And even seen this way,
nothing is missing.

84
00:05:04,589 --> 00:05:08,576
The mountain still stops the
climber, and still holds up the road.

85
00:05:09,427 --> 00:05:12,735
Third, a bat, a bee and an ant.

86
00:05:13,566 --> 00:05:16,407
Surely, though, the mountain is one.

87
00:05:16,487 --> 00:05:21,937
A human, a bat, a bee and an ant
all stand before the same mountain.

88
00:05:22,017 --> 00:05:23,717
Each sees it in its own way.

89
00:05:23,797 --> 00:05:26,693
But what they see is one
mountain, really there.

90
00:05:26,773 --> 00:05:29,071
The differences are only in the seeing.

91
00:05:29,151 --> 00:05:31,480
One world, many pictures of it.

92
00:05:32,301 --> 00:05:35,962
Or, and it is the biggest
or, ask each of them:

93
00:05:36,119 --> 00:05:37,424
is there a mountain there?

94
00:05:37,504 --> 00:05:41,464
The answers will not match,
because the worlds do not match.

95
00:05:42,278 --> 00:05:45,840
I see a bounded shape against
the sky, with a summit,

96
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:47,923
slopes and a base.

97
00:05:48,725 --> 00:05:53,169
A bat, finding its way by
echo, meets returning sound,

98
00:05:53,249 --> 00:05:55,986
with no clean edge where mountain stops.

99
00:05:56,793 --> 00:06:00,789
A bee, seeing in ultraviolet
among flowers and light,

100
00:06:00,869 --> 00:06:03,973
may hardly meet the mountain
as one thing at all.

101
00:06:04,775 --> 00:06:07,358
An ant takes a day to cross one boulder.

102
00:06:07,438 --> 00:06:13,273
It meets ridges of grain, warmth, and
the scent of its nest. Never a mountain.

103
00:06:14,094 --> 00:06:18,688
This is not four creatures looking at
one finished mountain from four angles.

104
00:06:18,768 --> 00:06:21,378
A different body singles
out a different world.

105
00:06:21,458 --> 00:06:25,835
The mountain, the one who meets it, and
the channel of meeting are designated

106
00:06:25,915 --> 00:06:29,657
together. None of them is
the bedrock under the others.

107
00:06:30,477 --> 00:06:33,331
And even seen this way,
nothing is missing.

108
00:06:33,411 --> 00:06:35,696
A rockfall can still crush the ant.

109
00:06:35,776 --> 00:06:40,736
Contact runs along its own channels,
gravity here and scent there,

110
00:06:40,816 --> 00:06:42,928
whether or not the creature knows it.

111
00:06:43,742 --> 00:06:46,448
Two ways of seeing, three times over.

112
00:06:46,528 --> 00:06:48,558
Which carries more valid truth?

113
00:06:49,373 --> 00:06:52,513
I test them by experience. Then by logic.

114
00:06:52,593 --> 00:06:55,262
Then I ask which one
explains how things work.

115
00:06:56,086 --> 00:07:01,468
By experience. Toss the apple again,
and look honestly. What is actually met?

116
00:07:01,548 --> 00:07:05,884
Coolness. Red. Weight.
The crunch. The name.

117
00:07:05,964 --> 00:07:09,340
At no point do I meet an apple
standing on its own behind them.

118
00:07:10,154 --> 00:07:14,005
The self-standing apple is
never found. It is supplied.

119
00:07:14,838 --> 00:07:18,929
The feeling that it is undeniably
there is real, as a feeling.

120
00:07:19,009 --> 00:07:21,801
But a feeling of solidity
is not a finding.

121
00:07:22,618 --> 00:07:24,345
The same goes for the mountain.

122
00:07:24,425 --> 00:07:27,416
I meet the view, the climb, the map.

123
00:07:27,496 --> 00:07:30,844
Never a mountain in itself,
apart from all of them.

124
00:07:31,670 --> 00:07:34,706
By logic. Take the first view at its word.

125
00:07:35,511 --> 00:07:38,651
An apple with its own fixed
nature could not ripen.

126
00:07:38,731 --> 00:07:42,170
It could not bruise, or
turn orange in candlelight.

127
00:07:42,250 --> 00:07:45,150
A fixed nature does not
change with conditions.

128
00:07:45,942 --> 00:07:50,916
A mountain with edges drawn from its own
side would show those edges to the bat and

129
00:07:50,996 --> 00:07:53,216
the ant. They meet none of them.

130
00:07:54,023 --> 00:07:58,889
And the one hidden mountain behind all
four creatures cannot be described at all.

131
00:07:58,969 --> 00:08:03,889
If it has features, a summit and slopes,
why do the bat and the ant meet none of

132
00:08:03,969 --> 00:08:09,722
them? If it has no features, a featureless
something cannot be what any of them meet.

133
00:08:10,597 --> 00:08:15,680
Finally, anything put forward as
self-standing undermines itself at once.

134
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:19,878
Even picking it out needs
contrast, context and a name.

135
00:08:19,958 --> 00:08:22,613
The very dependencies it claims to escape.

136
00:08:23,434 --> 00:08:27,525
By working. The first view says
things work because they are solid,

137
00:08:27,605 --> 00:08:29,441
and real from their own side.

138
00:08:29,521 --> 00:08:31,547
But what is fixed cannot interact.

139
00:08:31,627 --> 00:08:33,970
And what cannot interact cannot work.

140
00:08:34,790 --> 00:08:37,414
The second view explains
the working fully.

141
00:08:37,494 --> 00:08:39,439
An apple is tossed and eaten.

142
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:41,273
A mountain holds up a road.

143
00:08:41,353 --> 00:08:43,284
A rockfall crushes an ant.

144
00:08:43,364 --> 00:08:48,044
These are dependently arisen patterns,
meeting other patterns reliably.

145
00:08:48,845 --> 00:08:50,821
Working never needed an essence.

146
00:08:51,633 --> 00:08:55,656
So the first view is not the
truer one. It is the default one.

147
00:08:55,736 --> 00:08:58,930
It carries the weight of
habit, not of evidence.

148
00:08:59,010 --> 00:09:02,264
The second carries both
experience and logic.

149
00:09:03,085 --> 00:09:07,448
This does not make the everyday
claims false. The apple is an apple.

150
00:09:07,528 --> 00:09:11,460
The mountain is still there when
I look back. And I still say so.

151
00:09:12,281 --> 00:09:16,023
What fails is only the extra
claim: from its own side.

152
00:09:16,821 --> 00:09:18,507
Nothing that works is lost.

153
00:09:18,587 --> 00:09:21,107
Only a floor that was never there is gone.

154
00:09:21,926 --> 00:09:25,053
This is Part 1 of a series
on dependent arising.

155
00:09:25,133 --> 00:09:28,626
Here I have only set the two
ways of seeing side by side,

156
00:09:28,706 --> 00:09:30,533
and asked which one holds.

157
00:09:31,349 --> 00:09:36,867
In Part 2, The Illusion of the Given,
I take apart the belief left standing:

158
00:09:36,947 --> 00:09:39,910
that one world is already there, finished,

159
00:09:39,990 --> 00:09:42,492
and that beings only see it differently.

160
00:09:42,572 --> 00:09:46,228
It starts from one bowl of
liquid. A human sees water.

161
00:09:46,308 --> 00:09:51,545
A hungry ghost sees pus. A fish
sees its home. A god sees nectar.

